(7284019, 1134904, 25024, '<td valign="top">A lovely image, great lighting and use of DOF, well taken, good luck</td>', 'A lovely image, great lighting and use of DOF, well taken, good luck', '2014-11-11 11:47:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(7284020, 1133795, 25024, '<td valign="top">A well executed macro, good luck</td>', 'A well executed macro, good luck', '2014-11-11 11:48:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(7284026, 1133539, 159723, '<td valign="top">Amazing shot! This has a very 80s National Geographic feel about it for me. I mean that as a complement! :)</td>', 'Amazing shot! This has a very 80s National Geographic feel about it for me. I mean that as a complement! :)', '2014-11-11 12:24:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7284027, 1134820, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Simply a great catch - them against the decaying figure on the wall.<br/>2. Brilliantly exposed, with perfect toning.<br/>3. The dynamism of your subjects - not just their walking but how they are socially active as a trio.<br/>4. The contra directional arrow.<br/>5. The perfectly judged vignette.<br/>6. The shadows - theirs and the one on the wall to the extreme right.<br/> <br/>Brilliant stuff.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Simply a great catch - them against the decaying figure on the wall.2. Brilliantly exposed, with perfect toning.3. The dynamism of your subjects - not just their walking but how they are socially active as a trio.4. The contra directional arrow.5. The perfectly judged vignette.6. The shadows - theirs and the one on the wall to the extreme right. Brilliant stuff.', '2014-11-11 12:37:28.000000', NULL, 1),
