(7284034, 1133823, 100393, '<td valign="top">This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier) <br/> <br/>Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more. <br/> <br/>This is one of my 10s (I just bumped it from a 9) - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me:<br/> <br/>1. Horse pictures normally leave me cold, but this one is special.<br/>2. The extraordinary use of a deep depth of field. Inspired.<br/>3. The mixed use of high and low contrast, from bottom left to top right.<br/>4. The Icelandic feel!<br/>5. The communication of a physical context - the image is placed in the world, and with that us too as the viewer.<br/>6. That telegraph pole top right - it offers much in terms of offering scale and depth.<br/> <br/>Overall, this is magnificent.</td>', 'This image has caused me to stop and pay attention. That means it is in my 7-10 voting band. (Voted earlier)  Additionally, it is highly interesting/eclectic meaning it keeps me here long enough to offer a longer comment and a vote of 8 or more.  This is one of my 10s (I just bumped it from a 9) - I like it very much. Furthermore I think it enriches the DPC collective portfolio. Put simply, I wish we saw more stuff like this. Let me tell you why it pushes all the right buttons for me: 1. Horse pictures normally leave me cold, but this one is special.2. The extraordinary use of a deep depth of field. Inspired.3. The mixed use of high and low contrast, from bottom left to top right.4. The Icelandic feel!5. The communication of a physical context - the image is placed in the world, and with that us too as the viewer.6. That telegraph pole top right - it offers much in terms of offering scale and depth. Overall, this is magnificent.', '2014-11-11 12:55:18.000000', NULL, 1),
