(7284847, 1134855, 135629, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comment! There were quite a few good shots in this challenge, but I am also finding that when speaking generally of all challenges it''s really hard to grab above a 6 any more. I even earned a 2, that was a nice touch :) <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Techo:</b></div><hr/><i> Super beautiful shot. Got a 7 from me on first pass. Really like the stark contrast and graphic lines. Super surprised it didn''t edge out to at least a 6. I haven''t been around as much so maybe DPC tastes have shifted a bit but this one is eye candyish. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks for the comment! There were quite a few good shots in this challenge, but I am also finding that when speaking generally of all challenges it''s really hard to grab above a 6 any more. I even earned a 2, that was a nice touch :)  Originally posted by Techo: Super beautiful shot. Got a 7 from me on first pass. Really like the stark contrast and graphic lines. Super surprised it didn''t edge out to at least a 6. I haven''t been around as much so maybe DPC tastes have shifted a bit but this one is eye candyish. ', '2014-11-12 20:32:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7284849, 1134438, 109227, '<td valign="top">One of my higher scores; should have been much higher.  Love the candidness and the moment. Did not comment during voting; ran out of time.</td>', 'One of my higher scores; should have been much higher.  Love the candidness and the moment. Did not comment during voting; ran out of time.', '2014-11-12 20:35:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7284854, 1134923, 83149, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I want the focus to be sharper on her face.. and it seems blurred... maybe motion?<br/> <br/>Seems like the end of the log in the water is sharp and even the rock behind her.   <br/> <br/>Also, it looks uncomfortable to sit on that rock... nekkid!  LOL! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, it is motion.  It is a 10 second exposure, so I was pretty impressed that she did as well as she did.  <br/> <br/>I also had two 5s exposures, one was blurrier and the other was very sharp.  Unfortunately, another photog walked in front of my camera during the exposure (argghhh) and by that time, the model was done with trying to hold those poses on that rock (not really a rock, but the remnants of a foundation).  It was about 12 Celsius on this very rainy morning, she was quite the trooper.</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I want the focus to be sharper on her face.. and it seems blurred... maybe motion? Seems like the end of the log in the water is sharp and even the rock behind her.    Also, it looks uncomfortable to sit on that rock... nekkid!  LOL!   Yes, it is motion.  It is a 10 second exposure, so I was pretty impressed that she did as well as she did.   I also had two 5s exposures, one was blurrier and the other was very sharp.  Unfortunately, another photog walked in front of my camera during the exposure (argghhh) and by that time, the model was done with trying to hold those poses on that rock (not really a rock, but the remnants of a foundation).  It was about 12 Celsius on this very rainy morning, she was quite the trooper.', '2014-11-12 21:23:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(7284855, 1134424, 76335, '<td valign="top">Well, Deb''s important too... <br/> <br/>What can I say? I''m flattered, honored, maybe a little embarrassed. It was a truly an enjoyable evening. Deb''s a wonderful hostess, although I''m beginning to think her motives are selfish! Mine certainly are whenever I call her up to tell her I''ll be in town. But we have fun together -- along with whoever''s able to join us. <br/> <br/>And the photograph. I love it, of course. If "the photographer" were anyone else, I''d be terribly jealous. I suppose the pressure is on now to develop my film and see how this story ends.<br/> <br/>By the way, Deb, I have you beat in front page staleness: over <i>six</i> years. Sheesh! Were these children even born then? <br/></td>', 'Well, Deb''s important too...  What can I say? I''m flattered, honored, maybe a little embarrassed. It was a truly an enjoyable evening. Deb''s a wonderful hostess, although I''m beginning to think her motives are selfish! Mine certainly are whenever I call her up to tell her I''ll be in town. But we have fun together -- along with whoever''s able to join us.  And the photograph. I love it, of course. If "the photographer" were anyone else, I''d be terribly jealous. I suppose the pressure is on now to develop my film and see how this story ends. By the way, Deb, I have you beat in front page staleness: over six years. Sheesh! Were these children even born then? ', '2014-11-12 21:32:57.000000', NULL, 0),
